1
00:00:02,425 --> 00:00:03,968
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:04,802 --> 00:00:05,929
Earth...

3
00:00:06,679 --> 00:00:08,181
Fire...

4
00:00:09,015 --> 00:00:10,350
Air.

5
00:00:11,226 --> 00:00:15,271
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,355 --> 00:00:18,691
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,609 --> 00:00:22,612
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,695 --> 00:00:23,738
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,821 --> 00:00:25,615
But when the world
needed him most,

10
00:00:25,698 --> 00:00:26,741
He vanished.

11
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,409
100 years passed,

12
00:00:28,493 --> 00:00:30,995
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar―

13
00:00:31,079 --> 00:00:32,455
An airbender named Aang.

14
00:00:32,997 --> 00:00:35,124
And although his airbending
skills are great,

15
00:00:35,208 --> 00:00:37,794
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

16
00:00:37,877 --> 00:00:39,003
AANG: Oof!

17
00:00:39,087 --> 00:00:42,048
But I believe Aang can save the world.

18
00:01:00,904 --> 00:01:01,988
I can't believe it.

19
00:01:02,072 --> 00:01:03,865
I know the war has spread far,

20
00:01:03,949 --> 00:01:06,034
but Omashu always seemed...

21
00:01:06,117 --> 00:01:07,410
Untouchable.

22
00:01:07,702 --> 00:01:09,412
Up until now, it was.

23
00:01:09,746 --> 00:01:13,166
Now, Ba Sing Se is the only great
Earth Kingdom stronghold left.

24
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:14,876
KATARA: This is horrible.

25
00:01:15,877 --> 00:01:17,837
But we have to move on.

26
00:01:17,963 --> 00:01:18,964
No.

27
00:01:19,089 --> 00:01:20,799
I'm going in to find Bumi.

28
00:01:20,924 --> 00:01:22,092
SOKKA: Aang, stop!

29
00:01:22,217 --> 00:01:24,511
We don't even know if Bumi's still...

30
00:01:24,636 --> 00:01:26,846
What? If he's still what?

31
00:01:27,305 --> 00:01:28,306
Around.

32
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:31,101
I know you had
your heart set on Bumi,

33
00:01:31,184 --> 00:01:33,937
but there are other people
who can teach you earthbending.

34
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:35,981
This isn't about
finding a teacher.

35
00:01:36,314 --> 00:01:37,816
This is about
finding my friend.

36
00:01:42,946 --> 00:01:44,614
( GROWLING )

37
00:01:45,073 --> 00:01:46,283
SOKKA: A secret passage?

38
00:01:46,491 --> 00:01:48,785
Why didn't we just
use this last time?

39
00:01:49,077 --> 00:01:50,412
Ugh!

40
00:01:50,495 --> 00:01:51,955
Does that answer
your question?

41
00:01:53,665 --> 00:01:54,666
Ew!

42
00:02:00,588 --> 00:02:02,590
( RETCHING )

43
00:02:14,811 --> 00:02:16,354
That wasn't as bad as I thought.

44
00:02:22,068 --> 00:02:23,486
( SCREAMING )

45
00:02:27,490 --> 00:02:29,034
Aagh!

46
00:02:29,409 --> 00:02:30,702
They won't let go!

47
00:02:30,785 --> 00:02:31,786
Help!

48
00:02:31,870 --> 00:02:32,871
( GRUNTING )

49
00:02:33,121 --> 00:02:34,497
Stop making so much noise.

50
00:02:34,706 --> 00:02:36,249
It's just a purple pentapus.

51
00:02:37,125 --> 00:02:39,044
( GROANING )

52
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:41,963
Oh.

53
00:02:47,677 --> 00:02:48,845
MAN: Hey!

54
00:02:52,015 --> 00:02:53,933
What are you kids
doing out past curfew?

55
00:02:54,684 --> 00:02:55,769
KATARA: Sorry.

56
00:02:55,852 --> 00:02:57,228
We were just
on our way home.

57
00:03:00,357 --> 00:03:01,358
Wait.

58
00:03:01,441 --> 00:03:02,942
What's the matter with him?

59
00:03:03,026 --> 00:03:04,027
Uh...

60
00:03:04,110 --> 00:03:05,987
He has pentapox, sir.

61
00:03:07,906 --> 00:03:10,700
Um, it's highly contagious.

62
00:03:12,452 --> 00:03:13,620
( GROANING )

63
00:03:13,703 --> 00:03:16,164
It's so awful! I'm dying!

64
00:03:16,373 --> 00:03:17,415
KATARA: And deadly.

65
00:03:17,499 --> 00:03:20,085
Hey, I think I've heard of pentapox.

66
00:03:20,168 --> 00:03:22,003
Didn't your cousin Chang die of it?

67
00:03:22,087 --> 00:03:23,630
We better go wash our hands.

68
00:03:23,713 --> 00:03:24,798
And burn our clothes.

69
00:03:24,881 --> 00:03:26,299
( COUGHING )

70
00:03:27,092 --> 00:03:28,802
Thank you, sewer friend!

71
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,891
WOMAN: When tracking
your brother and uncle,

72
00:03:34,974 --> 00:03:36,601
traveling with
the royal procession

73
00:03:36,684 --> 00:03:38,895
may no longer be an option.

74
00:03:39,145 --> 00:03:41,022
May no longer be wise.

75
00:03:41,106 --> 00:03:44,317
BOTH: If you hope to keep
the element of surprise.

76
00:03:44,401 --> 00:03:45,610
AZULA: You're right.

77
00:03:45,693 --> 00:03:47,445
The royal procession is dead weight.

78
00:03:47,529 --> 00:03:49,030
If I want to catch my prey,

79
00:03:49,114 --> 00:03:51,074
I must be agile, nimble.

80
00:03:51,366 --> 00:03:53,660
I need a small, elite team.

81
00:03:54,035 --> 00:03:56,913
It's time to visit some old friends.

82
00:04:07,841 --> 00:04:09,926
KATARA: Let's find Bumi
and get out of here.

83
00:04:10,009 --> 00:04:11,719
Where would they
be keeping him?

84
00:04:11,803 --> 00:04:14,347
Somewhere he can't earthbend.

85
00:04:14,431 --> 00:04:16,141
Somewhere made of metal.

86
00:04:22,730 --> 00:04:24,482
There really is no fathoming

87
00:04:24,566 --> 00:04:25,733
the depths of my hatred

88
00:04:25,817 --> 00:04:27,318
for this place.

89
00:04:27,527 --> 00:04:30,071
Mai, your father was appointed governor.

90
00:04:30,447 --> 00:04:32,115
We're like royalty here.

91
00:04:32,198 --> 00:04:34,033
Be happy and enjoy it.

92
00:04:38,037 --> 00:04:39,747
MAN: The targets are approaching.

93
00:04:39,831 --> 00:04:41,124
Take them out.

94
00:04:41,583 --> 00:04:44,419
I thought my life was
boring in the Fire Nation,

95
00:04:44,502 --> 00:04:47,046
but this place is unbearably bleak.

96
00:04:47,297 --> 00:04:49,299
Nothing ever happens.

97
00:04:54,095 --> 00:04:55,597
( RUMBLING )

98
00:05:04,314 --> 00:05:05,523
The resistance!

99
00:05:13,865 --> 00:05:15,783
( GRUNTING )

100
00:05:35,303 --> 00:05:36,846
( YELLS )

101
00:05:38,264 --> 00:05:39,349
( SIGHS )

102
00:05:51,986 --> 00:05:52,987
Ty Lee,

103
00:05:53,071 --> 00:05:54,656
could that possibly be you?

104
00:05:56,074 --> 00:05:57,242
Azula!

105
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:03,706
It is so good to see you!

106
00:06:03,957 --> 00:06:06,167
Please, don't let me interrupt your...

107
00:06:06,251 --> 00:06:08,002
Whatever it is you were doing.

108
00:06:08,795 --> 00:06:09,963
Tell me...

109
00:06:10,046 --> 00:06:12,507
What is the daughter of a nobleman
doing here?

110
00:06:12,590 --> 00:06:14,342
Certainly our parents didn't send us

111
00:06:14,425 --> 00:06:16,177
to the Royal Fire Academy for Girls

112
00:06:16,261 --> 00:06:18,596
to end up in places like this.

113
00:06:21,641 --> 00:06:23,601
I have a proposition for you.

114
00:06:23,685 --> 00:06:24,936
I'm hunting a traitor.

115
00:06:25,228 --> 00:06:27,146
You remember my old fuddy-duddy uncle,

116
00:06:27,230 --> 00:06:28,231
don't you?

117
00:06:28,565 --> 00:06:30,984
Oh, yeah. He was so funny.

118
00:06:32,110 --> 00:06:34,862
I would be honored
if you would join me on my mission.

119
00:06:34,988 --> 00:06:36,281
Oh, I, uh...

120
00:06:36,364 --> 00:06:37,699
Would love to.

121
00:06:38,908 --> 00:06:39,951
But the truth is

122
00:06:40,034 --> 00:06:41,911
I'm really happy here.

123
00:06:41,995 --> 00:06:44,706
I mean, my aura has never been pinker.

124
00:06:45,081 --> 00:06:47,125
I'll take your word for it.

125
00:06:47,208 --> 00:06:48,960
Well, I wouldn't want you to give up

126
00:06:49,043 --> 00:06:51,462
the life you love just to please me.

127
00:06:52,338 --> 00:06:54,048
Thank you, Azula.

128
00:06:55,300 --> 00:06:56,968
Of course, before I leave,

129
00:06:57,051 --> 00:06:58,803
I'm going to catch your show.

130
00:06:58,886 --> 00:06:59,887
( GASPS )

131
00:06:59,971 --> 00:07:01,973
Uh, yeah, sure.

132
00:07:02,056 --> 00:07:03,141
Of course.

133
00:07:05,935 --> 00:07:08,563
AANG: So, is King Bumi with you guys?

134
00:07:09,105 --> 00:07:10,648
Is he leading the resistance?

135
00:07:11,024 --> 00:07:12,233
Of course not.

136
00:07:12,567 --> 00:07:13,776
The day of the invasion,

137
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:15,570
we readied ourselves for battle.

138
00:07:15,653 --> 00:07:17,572
We were prepared to defend our city,

139
00:07:17,655 --> 00:07:19,824
To fight for our lives
and for our freedom.

140
00:07:20,325 --> 00:07:22,869
But before we even had a chance,

141
00:07:22,952 --> 00:07:25,830
King Bumi surrendered.

142
00:07:33,463 --> 00:07:34,922
The day of the invasion,

143
00:07:35,006 --> 00:07:36,841
I asked King Bumi
what he wanted to do.

144
00:07:37,258 --> 00:07:38,926
He looked me
in the eye and said...

145
00:07:40,887 --> 00:07:42,847
I'm going to do nothing.

146
00:07:42,930 --> 00:07:43,931
Ha ha ha ha!

147
00:07:44,015 --> 00:07:45,308
( SNORT ) Ha ha ha.

148
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:47,310
It doesn't matter now.

149
00:07:47,602 --> 00:07:48,770
Fighting the Fire Nation

150
00:07:48,853 --> 00:07:50,188
is the only path to freedom.

151
00:07:50,563 --> 00:07:53,024
And freedom is worth dying for.

152
00:07:53,816 --> 00:07:55,818
Actually, there's another path to freedom.

153
00:07:55,902 --> 00:07:57,403
You could leave Omashu.

154
00:07:57,654 --> 00:07:59,280
You're directing all your energy

155
00:07:59,364 --> 00:08:00,573
to fight the Fire Nation,

156
00:08:00,823 --> 00:08:02,950
But you're outnumbered.
You can't win.

157
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,036
Now is the time to retreat

158
00:08:05,119 --> 00:08:06,913
so you can live to fight another day.

159
00:08:07,246 --> 00:08:08,706
You don't understand.

160
00:08:08,790 --> 00:08:09,999
They've taken our home,

161
00:08:10,083 --> 00:08:12,377
and we have to fight them at any cost!

162
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:13,628
I don't know, Yalo.

163
00:08:13,711 --> 00:08:15,046
Living to fight another day

164
00:08:15,129 --> 00:08:17,256
is starting to sound
pretty good to me.

165
00:08:17,465 --> 00:08:19,050
Yeah, I'm with the kid.

166
00:08:19,676 --> 00:08:20,802
( PEOPLE MURMURING )

167
00:08:24,180 --> 00:08:25,264
Fine.

168
00:08:25,348 --> 00:08:27,850
But there's thousands of citizens
that need to leave.

169
00:08:27,934 --> 00:08:29,602
How are we gonna get them all out?

170
00:08:29,686 --> 00:08:30,687
Suckers!

171
00:08:30,770 --> 00:08:31,854
( COOING )

172
00:08:32,730 --> 00:08:35,733
You're all about to come down
with a nasty case of pentapox.

173
00:08:48,621 --> 00:08:49,622
( GRUNTING )

174
00:08:52,750 --> 00:08:54,502
SOKKA: The marks make you look sick,

175
00:08:54,585 --> 00:08:55,962
but you gotta act sick, too!

176
00:08:56,379 --> 00:08:57,505
You gotta sell it.

177
00:08:58,214 --> 00:09:00,091
( GROANING )

178
00:09:03,553 --> 00:09:05,221
Now, that's what I'm talking about.

179
00:09:05,638 --> 00:09:07,265
Years of practice.

180
00:09:08,975 --> 00:09:10,059
Ok, everyone,

181
00:09:10,143 --> 00:09:11,269
into sick formation!

182
00:09:12,353 --> 00:09:13,521
( COOING )

183
00:09:13,604 --> 00:09:14,814
Aang, what are you doing?

184
00:09:14,897 --> 00:09:16,357
Aren't you coming with us?

185
00:09:16,441 --> 00:09:18,943
No. I'm not leaving until I find Bumi.

186
00:09:21,738 --> 00:09:23,823
Sorry, Momo. I'll feed you later.

187
00:09:30,496 --> 00:09:33,166
( PEOPLE GROANING )

188
00:09:50,141 --> 00:09:51,976
Plague! Plague!

189
00:09:53,269 --> 00:09:54,395
( CLANGING )

190
00:09:59,734 --> 00:10:01,527
What is going on down there?!

191
00:10:01,611 --> 00:10:02,820
I saw some kids yesterday

192
00:10:02,904 --> 00:10:04,322
who were sick with pentapox.

193
00:10:04,405 --> 00:10:05,490
It must have spread.

194
00:10:05,573 --> 00:10:06,824
Pentapox!

195
00:10:07,074 --> 00:10:09,243
Hmm. I'm pretty sure
I've heard of that.

196
00:10:09,952 --> 00:10:11,496
WOMAN: Oh, this is terrible.

197
00:10:11,579 --> 00:10:12,789
GUARD: What should we do?

198
00:10:12,872 --> 00:10:14,665
GOVERNOR: Drive them out of the city,

199
00:10:14,749 --> 00:10:16,125
but don't touch them.

200
00:10:16,209 --> 00:10:18,628
We have to rid the city of this disease.

201
00:10:20,505 --> 00:10:22,131
Fire flakes, dad?

202
00:10:22,757 --> 00:10:24,133
( GASPS )

203
00:10:24,217 --> 00:10:25,301
How awful!

204
00:10:36,395 --> 00:10:37,396
( PANTING )

205
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,564
Flopsie!

206
00:10:52,411 --> 00:10:53,412
( CHUCKLES )

207
00:10:53,496 --> 00:10:54,705
Come on, Flopsie.

208
00:10:54,789 --> 00:10:56,123
You gotta help me find Bumi.

209
00:10:56,207 --> 00:10:57,291
Yip, yip!

210
00:10:58,584 --> 00:11:01,254
Oh, I guess that
doesn't work with you.

211
00:11:01,337 --> 00:11:02,505
Let's go.

212
00:11:06,592 --> 00:11:08,135
( COOING )

213
00:11:10,847 --> 00:11:12,807
( BABY GIGGLING )

214
00:11:17,937 --> 00:11:19,689
( CHITTERING )

215
00:11:28,781 --> 00:11:30,324
( GIGGLING )

216
00:11:38,457 --> 00:11:40,126
Whoa!

217
00:11:51,804 --> 00:11:53,097
Wee!

218
00:12:01,355 --> 00:12:02,982
( CHITTERING )

219
00:12:03,774 --> 00:12:06,152
( PEOPLE GROANING )

220
00:12:15,494 --> 00:12:17,163
We're deeply honored

221
00:12:17,246 --> 00:12:18,789
to have the Fire Lord's daughter

222
00:12:18,873 --> 00:12:20,374
at our humble circus.

223
00:12:20,917 --> 00:12:22,418
And tell us if there's anything

224
00:12:22,501 --> 00:12:25,046
we can do to make
the show more enjoyable.

225
00:12:25,129 --> 00:12:26,172
I will.

226
00:12:32,929 --> 00:12:34,138
Incredible.

227
00:12:34,555 --> 00:12:35,806
Do you think she'll fall?

228
00:12:35,890 --> 00:12:37,058
Of course not.

229
00:12:37,141 --> 00:12:39,101
Then wouldn't it make it more interesting

230
00:12:39,185 --> 00:12:40,686
if you removed the net?

231
00:12:41,270 --> 00:12:43,105
Uh, the thing is...

232
00:12:43,189 --> 00:12:44,190
The performers―

233
00:12:44,273 --> 00:12:45,775
You're right. You're right.

234
00:12:45,858 --> 00:12:46,984
That's been done.

235
00:12:48,945 --> 00:12:50,029
I know.

236
00:12:50,112 --> 00:12:51,781
Set the net on fire.

237
00:12:51,864 --> 00:12:53,449
Of course, Princess.

238
00:13:01,666 --> 00:13:03,626
Brilliant. Just brilliant.

239
00:13:03,709 --> 00:13:04,919
Ooh!

240
00:13:05,002 --> 00:13:07,254
What kind of dangerous animals
do you have?

241
00:13:07,338 --> 00:13:10,216
Well, our circus boasts
the most exotic assortment―

242
00:13:10,299 --> 00:13:11,425
Release them all!

243
00:13:13,928 --> 00:13:15,054
( ELEPHANT TRUMPETS )

244
00:13:15,137 --> 00:13:16,555
( TIGER ROARS )

245
00:13:25,398 --> 00:13:26,941
We looked everywhere.

246
00:13:27,024 --> 00:13:28,651
No Bumi.

247
00:13:28,734 --> 00:13:30,403
( MOANS )

248
00:13:31,821 --> 00:13:33,114
MAN: We've got a problem.

249
00:13:33,197 --> 00:13:34,407
We just did a head count.

250
00:13:34,949 --> 00:13:37,201
KATARA: Oh, no.
Did someone get left behind?

251
00:13:37,743 --> 00:13:39,578
No. We have an extra.

252
00:13:45,751 --> 00:13:47,586
( WEEPING )

253
00:13:49,255 --> 00:13:52,633
GOVERNOR: So, the resistance
has kidnapped my son.

254
00:13:52,717 --> 00:13:55,469
Everything is so clever, so tricky―

255
00:13:55,553 --> 00:13:57,513
Just like their King Bumi.

256
00:13:57,596 --> 00:13:58,931
What do you want to do, sir?

257
00:14:05,438 --> 00:14:07,356
What an exquisite performance.

258
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,566
I can't wait to see

259
00:14:08,649 --> 00:14:10,234
how you'll top yourself tomorrow.

260
00:14:10,443 --> 00:14:11,444
I'm sorry, Azula,

261
00:14:11,527 --> 00:14:13,988
but unfortunately there
won't be a show tomorrow.

262
00:14:14,071 --> 00:14:15,114
Really?

263
00:14:15,781 --> 00:14:17,908
The universe is giving
me strong hints

264
00:14:17,992 --> 00:14:19,702
that it's time for a career change.

265
00:14:20,578 --> 00:14:22,246
I want to join you on your mission.

266
00:14:28,586 --> 00:14:29,587
( COOING )

267
00:14:34,050 --> 00:14:36,177
No! Bad Fire Nation baby.

268
00:14:36,552 --> 00:14:38,304
Waah!

269
00:14:39,930 --> 00:14:41,140
Oh, all right.

270
00:14:43,017 --> 00:14:44,935
( COOING )

271
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:47,772
Oh, you're so cute!

272
00:14:47,855 --> 00:14:48,856
Ooh!

273
00:14:48,939 --> 00:14:50,441
Sure, he's cute now.

274
00:14:50,524 --> 00:14:53,069
But when he's older,
he'll join the Fire Nation army.

275
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:55,112
You won't think he's so cute then.

276
00:14:55,196 --> 00:14:56,989
He'll be a killer.

277
00:14:57,239 --> 00:14:59,575
Does that look like
the face of a killer to you?

278
00:15:01,786 --> 00:15:03,621
( SQUAWKING )

279
00:15:05,164 --> 00:15:06,540
A messenger hawk.

280
00:15:08,584 --> 00:15:10,544
AANG: It's from the Fire Nation governor.

281
00:15:11,087 --> 00:15:12,963
He thinks we kidnapped his son.

282
00:15:13,047 --> 00:15:15,091
So, he wants to make a trade.

283
00:15:15,591 --> 00:15:16,634
His son...

284
00:15:16,717 --> 00:15:18,135
For King Bumi!

285
00:15:28,145 --> 00:15:30,981
SOKKA: You realize
we're probably walking right into a trap.

286
00:15:31,107 --> 00:15:32,108
I don't think so.

287
00:15:32,441 --> 00:15:34,401
I'm sure the governor wants his son back

288
00:15:34,485 --> 00:15:35,903
as much as we want Bumi.

289
00:15:35,986 --> 00:15:37,071
It's a new day.

290
00:15:37,446 --> 00:15:39,115
I have a good feeling about this.

291
00:15:48,749 --> 00:15:51,001
Please tell me you're
here to kill me.

292
00:15:52,461 --> 00:15:53,796
( CHUCKLES )

293
00:15:53,879 --> 00:15:55,381
It's great to see you, Mai.

294
00:15:56,257 --> 00:15:58,634
I thought you ran off
and joined the circus.

295
00:15:58,717 --> 00:16:00,136
You said it was your calling.

296
00:16:00,511 --> 00:16:03,389
Well, Azula called a little louder.

297
00:16:03,722 --> 00:16:04,765
I have a mission,

298
00:16:04,849 --> 00:16:06,267
and I need you both.

299
00:16:06,350 --> 00:16:07,351
Count me in.

300
00:16:07,810 --> 00:16:09,854
Anything to get me
out of this place.

301
00:16:10,771 --> 00:16:12,189
GOVERNOR: I apologize.

302
00:16:12,857 --> 00:16:15,025
You've come to Omashu at a difficult time.

303
00:16:15,401 --> 00:16:17,027
At noon, we're making a trade

304
00:16:17,111 --> 00:16:19,446
with the resistance to get Tom-Tom back.

305
00:16:19,530 --> 00:16:22,575
Yes, I'm so sorry to
hear about your son.

306
00:16:22,658 --> 00:16:24,577
But, really, what did you expect

307
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:27,329
by just letting all the citizens leave?

308
00:16:28,289 --> 00:16:30,416
My father has trusted you with this city,

309
00:16:30,499 --> 00:16:32,209
and you're making a mess of things.

310
00:16:32,293 --> 00:16:33,627
Forgive me, Princess.

311
00:16:34,211 --> 00:16:35,462
You stay here.

312
00:16:35,546 --> 00:16:37,131
Mai will handle the hostage trade

313
00:16:37,214 --> 00:16:39,216
so you don't have a chance to mess it up.

314
00:16:39,633 --> 00:16:41,302
AZULA: And there is no more Omashu.

315
00:16:41,385 --> 00:16:43,637
I am renaming it
in honor of my father.

316
00:16:43,762 --> 00:16:45,931
The city of New Ozai!

317
00:16:58,611 --> 00:16:59,612
( CHUCKLING )

318
00:17:01,447 --> 00:17:03,365
Hi, everybody!

319
00:17:05,951 --> 00:17:07,286
You brought my brother?

320
00:17:07,369 --> 00:17:08,495
AANG: He's here.

321
00:17:09,121 --> 00:17:10,539
We're ready to trade.

322
00:17:11,165 --> 00:17:13,375
I'm sorry, but a thought
just occurred to me.

323
00:17:13,459 --> 00:17:14,543
Do you mind?

324
00:17:14,627 --> 00:17:16,587
Of course not, Princess Azula.

325
00:17:16,670 --> 00:17:19,298
We're trading a two-year-old for a king―

326
00:17:19,381 --> 00:17:21,926
A powerful earthbending king.

327
00:17:22,801 --> 00:17:24,678
It just doesn't seem like a fair trade.

328
00:17:24,762 --> 00:17:25,763
Does it?

329
00:17:29,183 --> 00:17:30,184
You're right.

330
00:17:32,895 --> 00:17:34,146
The deal's off.

331
00:17:34,230 --> 00:17:35,397
Whoa!

332
00:17:36,023 --> 00:17:37,233
See you all later!

333
00:17:37,691 --> 00:17:39,193
( SNORT ) Ha ha ha.

334
00:17:39,693 --> 00:17:42,071
AANG: Bumi!

335
00:17:42,154 --> 00:17:43,572
( GRUNTS )

336
00:17:47,576 --> 00:17:48,577
( GRUNTS )

337
00:17:48,661 --> 00:17:50,079
The Avatar.

338
00:17:52,164 --> 00:17:53,958
My lucky day.

339
00:18:00,256 --> 00:18:02,132
Aang! Is that you?

340
00:18:02,216 --> 00:18:03,842
Where did you
come from?

341
00:18:04,218 --> 00:18:06,762
Hang on. We're gonna get you out of here.

342
00:18:14,645 --> 00:18:16,522
We've gotta get the baby out of here!

343
00:18:17,481 --> 00:18:19,108
Way ahead of you.

344
00:18:22,486 --> 00:18:23,821
( GRUNTING )

345
00:18:39,128 --> 00:18:40,129
( SCREAMS )

346
00:18:46,093 --> 00:18:48,512
Aang! Stop your blowing for a minute.

347
00:18:52,516 --> 00:18:53,517
( GROWLING )

348
00:18:53,642 --> 00:18:54,935
BUMI: Now hold on just a―

349
00:18:55,019 --> 00:18:56,645
Aagh!

350
00:19:12,119 --> 00:19:13,203
( LAUGHING )

351
00:19:13,287 --> 00:19:14,496
It's just like old times,

352
00:19:14,580 --> 00:19:15,581
Isn't it, Bumi?

353
00:19:15,664 --> 00:19:17,833
Aang, I need to talk to you!

354
00:19:17,916 --> 00:19:19,626
It's good to see you, too!

355
00:19:32,222 --> 00:19:33,223
Aagh!

356
00:19:50,074 --> 00:19:51,325
Phew!

357
00:19:52,868 --> 00:19:53,869
Aagh!

358
00:20:03,462 --> 00:20:04,463
( GRUNTS )

359
00:20:08,258 --> 00:20:10,386
( GRUNTING )

360
00:20:16,975 --> 00:20:19,228
How are you gonna fight
without your bending?

361
00:20:20,270 --> 00:20:21,397
( GASPS )

362
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:22,564
( GRUNTS )

363
00:20:22,898 --> 00:20:23,941
I seem to manage!

364
00:20:27,152 --> 00:20:28,779
( SCREAMS )

365
00:20:31,532 --> 00:20:32,616
There's Aang!

366
00:20:32,699 --> 00:20:33,867
We can catch him!

367
00:20:38,872 --> 00:20:40,082
Hang on, Bumi!

368
00:20:40,165 --> 00:20:41,375
Our ride's here!

369
00:20:45,462 --> 00:20:46,547
( GRUNTING )

370
00:20:47,131 --> 00:20:48,465
Aang!

371
00:20:51,552 --> 00:20:52,803
Oof!

372
00:20:57,850 --> 00:20:58,851
( GRUNTS )

373
00:21:17,786 --> 00:21:18,871
You could earthbend...

374
00:21:19,246 --> 00:21:20,414
All along?!

375
00:21:20,539 --> 00:21:22,666
Well, they didn't cover my face.

376
00:21:23,542 --> 00:21:24,710
( GRUNTS )

377
00:21:26,753 --> 00:21:27,963
I don't understand.

378
00:21:28,046 --> 00:21:29,715
Why didn't you free yourself?

379
00:21:30,048 --> 00:21:32,259
Why did you surrender
when Omashu was invaded?

380
00:21:32,342 --> 00:21:34,261
What's the matter with you, Bumi?!

381
00:21:34,344 --> 00:21:35,846
Listen to me, Aang.

382
00:21:36,138 --> 00:21:38,474
There are options in fighting called jing.

383
00:21:38,557 --> 00:21:41,602
It's a choice of how
you direct your energy.

384
00:21:42,060 --> 00:21:44,146
I know! Positive jing
when you're attacking,

385
00:21:44,229 --> 00:21:46,190
and negative jing when you're retreating.

386
00:21:46,565 --> 00:21:49,276
And neutral jing, when you do nothing.

387
00:21:49,359 --> 00:21:51,111
There are three jings?

388
00:21:51,195 --> 00:21:53,238
Well, technically, there are 85.

389
00:21:53,322 --> 00:21:55,407
But let's just focus on the third.

390
00:21:55,824 --> 00:21:58,785
Neutral jing is the key
to earthbending.

391
00:21:58,869 --> 00:22:01,205
It involves listening and waiting

392
00:22:01,288 --> 00:22:03,582
for the right moment to strike.

393
00:22:03,916 --> 00:22:06,084
That's why you surrendered, isn't it?

394
00:22:06,168 --> 00:22:08,670
Yes, and it's why I can't leave now.

395
00:22:10,756 --> 00:22:13,800
I guess I need to find someone else
to teach me earthbending.

396
00:22:13,884 --> 00:22:15,385
Your teacher will be someone

397
00:22:15,469 --> 00:22:17,763
who has mastered neutral jing.

398
00:22:17,846 --> 00:22:19,264
You need to find someone

399
00:22:19,348 --> 00:22:22,976
who waits and listens before striking.

400
00:22:23,101 --> 00:22:24,269
-( COOING )
- Hey, Momo.

401
00:22:24,603 --> 00:22:27,147
Momo's mastered
a few jings himself.

402
00:22:27,773 --> 00:22:28,941
( SQUEALS )

403
00:22:29,024 --> 00:22:30,275
Good-bye, Aang.

404
00:22:30,359 --> 00:22:33,153
I'll see you when the time is right.

405
00:22:33,278 --> 00:22:35,489
( LAUGHING )

406
00:22:35,614 --> 00:22:38,158
( SNORTING )

407
00:22:42,329 --> 00:22:45,165
So, we're tracking down
your brother and uncle, huh?

408
00:22:45,249 --> 00:22:47,459
It'll be interesting seeing Zuko again,

409
00:22:47,543 --> 00:22:48,877
won't it, Mai?

410
00:22:49,670 --> 00:22:52,506
It's not just Zuko And Iroh anymore.

411
00:22:52,631 --> 00:22:54,716
We have a third target now.

412
00:23:00,556 --> 00:23:02,432
( COOING )

413
00:23:05,185 --> 00:23:06,770
( GURGLING )

414
00:23:06,853 --> 00:23:07,980
( GASPS )

415
00:23:08,105 --> 00:23:09,940
Tom-tom!
